/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:20:    "main_doc_head": "Fill the frame with recolored sprites after decoding frame colors through a lookup table and then a complement rule.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background canvas contains one gray rectangular frame whose interior holds solid query-colored placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame are complementary-color sprite templates, the usual overlapping 3x4 recolor legends keyed by\n  intermediate colors, and a separate top-left lookup legend whose 2x2 tiles decode query color -> intermediate color.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:30:    "main_doc_head": "Fill the framed placeholders with matched sprites, then recolor them through split edge legends.\n\nInput structure:\n- A single gray rectangular frame encloses solid source-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n- Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template per placeholder color.\n- Legend entries are split across the grid boundary: top or left fragments show transformed shape clues in\n  one shared ink color, while the paired bottom or right fragments show only the target recolor.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:40:    "main_doc_head": "Copy two-color sprites into the frame by matching their dominant color and recoloring only that color class.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background grid contains one rectangular gray frame whose interior holds solid NxN placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame there is one two-color sprite per placeholder color, plus compact two-color legend glyphs that\n  encode placeholder-color -> target-color mappings.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:50:    "main_doc_head": "Fill framed cavities with quadrant-rotated sprites, then recolor them using the outside legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses a solid gray tray whose only non-gray interior regions are\n  rectangular bg cavities.\n- Outside the frame sit one source-colored sprite template per source color and one compact\n  two-color legend block per source color.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:60:    "main_doc_head": "Rebuild a framed sprite mosaic from edge-projected anchors, then recolor it with the legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background-filled canvas contains one rectangular frame whose interior starts empty.\n- Just outside the frame, a narrow band on the left carries colored row markers and a narrow band\n  on the top carries colored column markers.\n- Elsewhere outside the frame sit one sprite template per source color and one compact two-color\n  legend per source color."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:70:    "main_doc_head": "Rebuild the framed output by combining color-matched sprites, quadrant-based rotation, and rotating multicolor legend tiles.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid-color square placeholder blocks arranged on a regular grid.\n- Outside the frame sit one monochrome sprite template per placeholder color and one opaque rectangular legend per color; each legend has a source-color tag column and an NxN multicolor pattern sample.\n\nRule:\n- Detect the frame, all placeholder blocks inside it, the matching-color sprite masks outside it, and the pattern tile stored in each legend."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:80:    "main_doc_head": "Grow recolored sprite outlines from interior anchor pixels, then cancel outline overlaps by XOR.\n\nInput structure:\n- The scene has a background, one rectangular gray frame, and several single-pixel color anchors inside that frame.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each anchor color, plus one compact two-color legend glyph that maps each source color to its final output color.\n\nRule:\n- Detect the frame, the anchor pixels inside it, the same-color sprite template outside it, and the legend-based recoloring map."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:90:    "main_doc_head": "Replace framed placeholders with counted sprites and recolor them via a filtered count legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n- Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n- The top-left band contains compact monochrome legend entries whose colored pixel counts encode lookup keys,\n  and some of those legend counts are distractors unused by any real sprite.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:110:    "main_doc_head": "Place one recolored sprite at a time, letting earlier placements block later searches.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses repeated solid placeholder blocks of several colors on a\n  regular lattice.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template per placeholder color plus one two-color legend\n  per placeholder color; in generated samples the sprites form a readable row above the frame.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:120:    "main_doc_head": "Stamp recolored sprites into multiple marked frames using edge-color coordinates and a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background, 2-3 separate gray frames whose borders carry colored row/column markers, and uniform guide blocks inside each frame.\n- Outside the combined framed area: sprite shapes (one per source color) and compact legend glyphs mapping each source color to an output color.\n\nRule:\n- Find every marked frame, collect its guide-block bboxes, and read same-color markers from opposite edges of that frame."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:130:    "main_doc_head": "Fill a partitioned frame with recolored sprites whose orientation is decided per chamber.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid placeholder blocks, and a gray divider splits the frame interior into left/right chambers.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template per placeholder color plus two legend groups, one fully left of the frame and one fully right of it.\n\nRule:\n- Detect the frame, recover the two chambers from the internal divider, and assign every placeholder block to exactly one chamber."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:140:    "main_doc_head": "Fill framed cavities with recolored sprites chosen only by exact cavity size.\n\nInput structure:\n- A bg canvas contains one gray framed tray whose interior is mostly gray, except for several rectangular bg\n  cavities of varying sizes.\n- Outside the tray are monochrome sprite templates and compact two-color legend glyphs. The sprite colors match\n  legend source colors, but they do not appear inside the tray.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:150:    "main_doc_head": "Stamp external sprites into the frame, then recolor them by a mirrored bottom-right spatial legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- The canvas background contains one gray rectangular frame with solid colored placeholders inside.\n- The bottom-right corner of the whole canvas contains a fixed 5x5 legend panel with four colored 2x2 blocks.\n- Outside the frame and outside that corner panel: one sprite template per placeholder color.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:160:    "main_doc_head": "Recolor and place outlined hollow sprites into the framed workspace.\n\nInput structure:\n- The canvas has one rectangular gray frame whose interior contains solid-color placeholder blocks.\n- Outside the frame, each placeholder color has a same-color sprite template; these templates are hollow shapes with enclosed background holes.\n- The outside area also contains compact two-color legend glyphs that map placeholder colors to their final output colors.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:170:    "main_doc_head": "Copy same-colored sprite templates into a framed placeholder layout while leaving all outside objects visible.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background, one rectangular gray frame, and solid colored placeholder blocks inside the frame.\n- Outside the frame: one real sprite template per placeholder color plus a compact two-color legend block for each color.\n\nRule:\n- Find the frame and the placeholder blocks inside it."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:180:    "main_doc_head": "Place recolored sprites into a framed region by combining connector selection with anchor alignment.\n\nInput structure:\n- One rectangular frame on a background, with single-pixel source-colored targets inside the frame.\n- Each target slot also has a small connector glyph in the two rows above it.\n- Outside the frame: sprite templates whose bodies contain one gray anchor pixel and whose own\n  connector glyph sits directly above the body, plus the usual small two-color legends.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:200:    "main_doc_head": "Recolor outside sprites through a color table before placing them into the framed region.\n\nInput structure:\n- A background canvas contains one gray rectangular frame whose interior holds solid NxN target-color placeholders.\n- Outside the frame are source-colored sprite templates and, in the upper-left corner, a compact Kx4 color\n  lookup table with rows of the form [src, src, tgt, tgt].\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:220:    "main_doc_head": "Fill a framed tray by shape-matching guide markers to external sprites, rotating them by cavity quadrant, and recoloring them through the outside legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses a gray tray whose occupied slots each contain a sparse guide marker in the slot's upper-left corner and a square bg cavity in the slot's lower-right corner.\n- Outside the frame sit one unrotated source-colored sprite template per shape and one compact two-color legend block per source color.\n\nRule:\n- Detect every cavity and the same-size marker placed exactly one cavity-width above and left of it, then normalize the marker's unrotated shape."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:230:    "main_doc_head": "Rebuild the framed output by combining split edge legends, shape matching up to transform, and quadrant-based placement rotation.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses solid placeholder blocks of one shared square size.\n- Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template per placeholder color.\n- Along the outer boundary, legend entries are scattered across different edges: the top or left fragment shows a silhouette in one common legend-ink color, while the opposite bottom or right fragment supplies the target color for the same span.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:240:    "main_doc_head": "Copy two-color sprites into the frame, but recolor only their dominant-color pixels when a legend entry exists.\n\nInput structure:\n- One rectangular gray frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks laid out on the background.\n- Outside the frame there is one connected two-color sprite for every placeholder color; the larger-area color is\n  the sprite's primary color and matches the placeholder.\n- Also outside the frame are compact two-color legend glyphs for only some placeholder colors, so the legend set is\n  intentionally incomplete."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:250:    "main_doc_head": "Stamp frame-selected patterned sprites into a framed region using outside sprite templates and paired multicolor legends.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background, one rectangular non-gray frame, and solid square placeholder blocks inside that frame.\n- Outside the frame: one monochrome sprite template per placeholder color, plus two opaque N x (N+1) legends for each source color.\n  Each legend starts with a uniform source-color column and its right N x N tile is either a striped or checkerboard pattern sample.\n\nRule:"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:260:    "main_doc_head": "Replace repeated target clusters by one nearest recolored sprite inside the frame.\n\nInput structure:\n- A gray rectangular frame encloses several small same-color connected clusters instead of solid\n  placement blocks, and a source color can appear on multiple interior clusters.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template per source color plus the usual overlapping\n  two-color legend that tells which final color each source color should become.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:270:    "main_doc_head": "Replace the frame's solid placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them by an area-coded 2x2 legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- One gray rectangular frame sits on a background canvas; inside it are solid NxN placeholder blocks on a regular grid.\n- Outside the frame there is one sprite template per placeholder color.\n- Outside the frame there are also several opaque legend strips. Each strip is built by repeating the same 2x2 color matrix\n  horizontally: left column = shared counting color, right column = that strip's output color.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:280:    "main_doc_head": "Place legend-recolored sprites into a framed region using single-cell anchors, then resolve overlaps.\n\nInput structure:\n- A single gray rectangular frame surrounds sparse colored anchor pixels on a bg interior.\n- Outside the frame, each anchor color has one same-color sprite template and one compact two-color legend block.\n\nRule:\n- Match each inside-frame anchor color to the outside sprite of the same color and to its legend-defined target color."
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:290:    "main_doc_head": "Stamp external sprites into the frame, then recolor them from a two-layer spatial legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- The canvas background contains one gray rectangular frame with solid colored placeholders inside.\n- The top-left corner contains a fixed legend rectangle made of two aligned 2x2 panels:\n  a left base-color panel of solid swatches and a right modifier panel of glyphs.\n- Outside the frame and outside that reserved legend area: one sprite template per placeholder color.\n"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/edb79dae_review_extract.json:300:    "main_doc_head": "Reconstruct rectangles from diagonal markers, stamp them from anchor pixels inside a frame, then recolor them.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a bg color, one rectangular gray frame, and single-pixel colored anchors inside that frame.\n- Outside the frame, each anchor color appears as two same-color pixels at opposite corners of a rectangle bbox.\n- Small overlapping two-color legend glyphs outside the frame map each anchor/source color to its output color.\n\nRule:"
