/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:9:#    - D5/1 change: after geometry is known, parallel chains exchange colors depth-by-depth. The
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:13:#    - Small example: chain A has source colors [2,4], chain B has [3,8]. Geometry stays the same.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:14:#      Output chain colors become A->[3,8], B->[2,4]. Meanwhile every input sprite location turns
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:16:#      output simultaneously shows the swapped assembled chains and the gray source traces.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:19:#    - A single chain would make color swap invisible, so the generator always builds exactly two
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:20:#      adjacent parallel chains on the same side of the bar.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:21:#    - Unequal chain depth would create unmatched pieces and weaken the swap rule, so both chains
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:33:#      so sorting chains by strip coordinate gives a stable adjacent pairing humans can also see.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:38:#    - Generator stays output-first: build valid chains first, then scatter source sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:44:#      source silhouettes; output assembled chains near the bar with exchanged colors. Because the two
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:45:#      chains are parallel and same-depth, the color swap is not arbitrary recoloring.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:47:#      adjacency and depth order along the chain.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:52:#    - Generator keeps source sprites away from the bar and from each other, preventing shadow/chain
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:57:#    - Every sample contains two chains with repeated depth structure, giving enough support to infer
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:58:#      "same depth across adjacent chains swaps color".
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:63:#    - Assumption: exactly two real chains exist and lie on the same side. Generator constructs that.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:64:#    - Assumption: chains have equal depth so depth-wise swapping is total rather than partial.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/9/code.py:66:#    - Assumption: source shadows do not overwrite assembled chains. Generator scatters pieces away
